{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "kind": "help-article",
  "title": "Configuring a Service Connector",
  "source": {
    "url": "https://help.zscaler.com/deception/configuring-service-connector",
    "node": "1542375",
    "revision": "3221733",
    "updated": "2026-09-22",
    "updated_basis": "pdf-last-modified"
  },
  "captured_at": "2026-11-03",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "You can configure a Service Connector on your Windows or Linux system by downloading and running the Service Connector executables from the Zscaler Deception Admin Portal."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Prerequisites",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Before you configure a Service Connector, make sure that you have:"
    },
    {
      "item": "An always-on system or endpoint that can run the Service Connector executable.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Network reachability from the server or endpoint to the Deception Admin Portal.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Network reachability from the system running the Service Connector or endpoint to the SIEM solution.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "heading": "Configuring a Service Connector",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Follow these steps to configure a Service Connector:"
    },
    {
      "item": "Step 1: Add a Service Connector",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Go to Orchestrate > Service Connectors.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          17
        ],
        [
          20,
          38
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Add Connector.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          19
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "In the Service Connector Details window:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          32
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Under General, enter the Name of the Service Connector.",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          13
        ],
        [
          25,
          29
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If you plan to forward events from an IBM QRadar SIEM server to the Deception Service Connector, under Syslog Receiver:",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          103,
          118
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select a syslog Source Type from the drop-down menu.",
      "depth": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          16,
          27
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Add the IP addresses of SIEM servers to the Source Allowed IPs list.",
      "depth": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          44,
          62
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Save.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "API tokens are generated.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "In the API Token generated window, click the Windows or Linux tab, and copy the API token.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          26
        ],
        [
          45,
          52
        ],
        [
          56,
          61
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "For security purposes, the token is not displayed again after closing the window.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Close.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 6,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          11
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "The Service Connector is added to the Service Connectors table.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          38,
          56
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Step 2: Download and Run the Service Connector Executable",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Service Connectors page, click Download Connector.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          25
        ],
        [
          38,
          56
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select a Service Connector executable from the drop-down menu.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "The executable is downloaded to your local system.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "In the command prompt, run the following command to configure the Service Connector on your local system:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3
    },
    {
      "item": "Windows",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Linux",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Without proxy:",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "SiemConnector-windows.exe --host=<Deception Admin Portal instance> --api=<API Token> -v",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "With proxy:",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "./SiemConnector-windows.exe --host=<Deception Admin Portal instance> --api=<API Token> --proxy=http://<username:password@proxy-server:proxy-port>",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Without proxy:",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "SiemConnector-linux --host=<Deception Admin Portal instance> --api=<API Token> -v",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "With proxy:",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "./SiemConnector-linux --host=<Deception Admin Portal instance> --api=<API Token> --proxy=http://<username:password@proxy-server:proxy-port>",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "You can configure a service or daemon to start the Service Connector at boot and keep the Service Connector running.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "After you configure a Service Connector, you can integrate the Deception with a supported SIEM solution.",
      "depth": 0
    }
  ]
}
